    "id": "regenesis",
    "title": "Regenesis: aging as loss of phase",
    "category": "research",
    "collection": "biophysic",
    "type": "Collection introduction",
    "date": "2026-09-08",
    "description": "What is actually lost when an organism stops maintaining itself, and what restoration would therefore have to mean.",
    "tone": "sage",
    "body": "<h2>What does it mean to restore organisation?</h2>\n<p>Regenesis holds the biological side of Science Coherence: aging, regeneration, cellular organisation, and what happens where the loop meets tissue. Its starting point is a question about how an organism maintains itself — and what is actually lost when that maintenance fails.</p>\n<p>The framework's answer reframes the question. An organism is not a structure that happens to be maintained; it is maintenance holding a shape, a standing wave sustained by continuous integration. So senescence is not first of all an accumulation of damage. Damage accumulates in any open system. What changes is the rate of re-cohering — aging as loss of phase, in which subsystems that once updated together drift apart and the correction that used to close the gap stops closing it.</p>\n<h2>The same failure at every scale</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Chromatin.</strong> Heterochromatin de-condenses; what was locked becomes readable; parasitic sequence wakes.</li>\n<li><strong>Methylome.</strong> Marks drift from their coordinates — hypermethylation where suppression is needed, global loss where structure is needed.</li>\n<li><strong>Interfacial water.</strong> Structured phase collapses into bulk, and with it the proton conduction the whole arrangement depends on.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each is local variation no longer respecting what holds globally. That is one description, not three.</p>\n<h2>The consequence</h2>\n<p>If dissolution is loss of phase, restoration is re-phasing — and re-phasing is something the loop already does to itself. The work is not to supply the organism with something foreign, but to hold the conditions under which its own selection can run coherently again.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#/protocol\">The operating document</a> is that consequence carried out in full, and <a href=\"#/read/time-crystalline-v2\">the framework</a> is the architecture it rests on.</p>\n<h2>Open questions</h2>\n<p>How should phase relation be measured across biological scales, at the precision the claim requires? What distinguishes coordination from coincidence in a system where everything is coupled to everything? Which observations would force the model to change? These organise the collection.</p>\n",
